1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Secret Service is a drama, war film directed by Hugh Ford.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Lewis Dumont, a Northern officer in the American Civil War, works undercover behind Confederate lines in an
attempt to lead Southern forces away from an area in which a Northern attack is planned.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
But Dumont falls in love with a Southern girl and when she proves
useful to his plan, his conscience begins to tear at him.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Major Lewis K. Dumont, played by Robert Warwick.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Edith Varney, played by Wanda Hawley.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
General Harrison Randolph, played by Theodore Roberts.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Mrs. Varney, played by Edythe Chapman.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Lieutenant Howard Varney, played by Raymond Hatton.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Wilfred Varney, played by Casson Ferguson.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Secret Service is a lost 1919 American silent American Civil War drama
film starring Robert Warwick and directed by Hugh Ford.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
It was produced by Famous Players–Lasky and distributed by Paramount Pictures.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Based on the play Secret Service by William Gillette (New York, 5 Oct
1896), it was remade as a talking picture by RKO in 1931.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
One of the story’s chief plot twists is referenced in the 1923 short story "Devil
Cat", featuring Carroll John Daly’s hard boiled detective Race Williams.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The tone is emotional.
